<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Rive version="1" kind="fragment">
    <!--
      Creative Cat — master character (Cat 2A.1, reference-vector migration).

      Geometry is copied verbatim from rive/references/scene.rml, the traced
      vector source, and transformed with ONE global mapping:

        CAT_SOURCE_BOUNDS  x 10..170, y 2..203   (160 x 201, scene units)
        MASTER_SCALE       2.3
        MASTER_OFFSET      49, 20.25

      That mapping is locked and must be reused for every later Cat 2 phase
      (eyes, muzzle, whiskers, body, paws, tail). No per-part scaling.

      The source draws ears before the head, so the ears sit on top of the head
      fill; the sibling order below preserves that, which is what keeps the
      ear/head junction seamless under a fill-on-fill construction.

      Static artwork only: no state machine, no view model, no animation.
      Imported: head fill + 4 left-ear shapes + 4 right-ear shapes + 9 head
      surface shapes (crown, two shades, two cheek lights, four fur marks).
      Absent by design: whiskers, body, paws, tail, ball.

      Paint order: surface details first (top), then the head fill, then the
      ears. In the source file the details come after the head, i.e. they are
      painted above it; RML inverts sibling order, so they are declared first.
    -->
    <Artboard name="CreativeCatMaster" id="0:2" styleId="0:5" width="512" height="512">
        <LayoutComponentStyle name="Artboard Style" id="0:5" />

